## Interjection twins of content words (review 2, MLEX2-01). Zemberek lists commands, vocatives
## and exclamations as interjections beside the noun, adjective or adverb they are (ileri,
## devam, ay, teslim, ölüm, amca, kamera). The corpus prior cannot tell the two apart, so the
## interjection often won the best reading: 0.55 % of court tokens. UD Turkish's train and dev
## splits tag none of these forms INTJ in 10 % or more of their uses (most never); the
## interjections they do tag so (haydi, hadi, eyvah, of, ah, ha, aferin, e, a, evet, hayır,
## ya, neyse ...) keep theirs, as do exclamations UD lacks (amin, oley, zinhar, vallahi).
## The rare true interjection uses of the others lose to their content reading: ay "ouch", oy,
## tabi (mostly tabii misspelt, which keeps its own readings).
acayip [P:Interj]
ahbap [P:Interj]
alarga [P:Interj]
amca [P:Interj]
ana [P:Interj]
