## Names only proper-from-corpus.dict lists that are common words (MLEX2-03): the analyzer has
## a common reading for them, and the court and RagTurk samples write them in lower case at
## least as often as capitalised (ten times as often where TRmorph's or Google's name lists
## have them: Edip, Gerçek, Sona, Verdi), or, seen fewer than ten times, they are a common
## root with a suffix (Ruha, Satar). Their capitals were sentence-initial: Açık, Kadar, Banka,
## Danışmanlık read as names before. Names without a common reading (temyizen, usuli) wait
